# Test cards. One per line: title, the first message (sent as written), notes for the simulated user and the judge (free text), up to 10 user messages.
{"id": "tests/01_movie_weekend", "title": "Movie weekend", "opening": "Need to find a good movie this weekend, primetime, find me good seats.", "brief": "What is going on: my partner and I want a movie night this Saturday near where I live.\nWhat I want: two or three movies playing this Saturday around 7-8pm near where I live, with showtimes and a theater.\nDetails I give only when asked: Saturday, 7 to 8pm start; two people; near where I live, 20 minutes max; likes what I like to watch; do not buy tickets; show me showtimes and which seats are good.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-19"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least two specific showtimes on Saturday evening at a named theater near where I live, with a seat suggestion, no tickets bought"}
{"id": "tests/02_concerts_this_month", "title": "Concerts this month", "opening": "I enjoy indie, indie rock, alternative rock, and pop concerts. Some of my favorite artists are The Lumineers, Arctic Monkeys, and Taylor Swift. Could you help me find concerts this month that are not too expensive to go to?", "brief": "What is going on: I want a concert this month within an hour of where I live; weeknights are fine except the evenings in the calendar.\nWhat I want: three concerts this month near where I live under $80 a ticket that fit the calendar.\nDetails I give only when asked: within an hour of where I live; under $80 a ticket, two tickets; busy evenings: my calendar; smaller venues are fine; no buying; show me the options and the cheapest way to get tickets.\nIn order: three concerts this month near where I live in those genres under $80; then which ones fit my calendar; then the cheapest legitimate ticket source for the best one.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-50"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least two named concerts this month near where I live under $80 that do not clash with the calendar, with where to buy"}
{"id": "tests/03_pool_tomorrow", "title": "Pool tomorrow", "opening": "Find me a pool that I can swim at tomorrow, and write me a workout", "brief": "What is going on: I used to swim regularly and wants to get back in the water tomorrow morning.\nWhat I want: a pool near where I live with drop-in access tomorrow morning and a 45-minute intermediate workout.\nDetails I give only when asked: tomorrow morning, 9 to 11 free; lives in where I live; intermediate swimmer, two years off; wants 45 minutes; no membership, wants drop-in or a day pass.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-7"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "a named pool near where I live with tomorrow-morning drop-in hours and a workout written as sets with distances"}
{"id": "tests/04_sf_marathon", "title": "Sf marathon", "opening": "I am running the SF Marathon in 2027. This is my first marathon. I can run twice a week now (Saturday and Sunday) and ramp up to 3 and 4 times a week as I get closer. I ran a half marathon before and 3 miles a week every week. Can you help me make a marathon training plan?", "brief": "What is going on: I want a plan they can actually follow around work (my weekly routine).\nWhat I want: a week-by-week plan from now to the race, starting at two runs a week, with the long run on Sunday.\nDetails I give only when asked: long runs on Sunday, easy run Saturday; half-marathon time was about 2h10; no injuries, but knees get sore above 15 miles a week early on; wants it as a page or document I can keep; add the long-run days to my calendar only if you ask first.\nIn order: a phased week-by-week plan to race day with weekly mileage; then the long-run progression and when the third and fourth day start; then a shareable page or document with the plan.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-56"], "leaves": "a page or document", "done_when": "a week-by-week plan to the race with weekly mileage and long-run progression exists in a page or document the user can open"}
{"id": "tests/05_wedding_gift", "title": "Wedding gift", "opening": "My best friend just got married. What should I get her as a wedding gift?", "brief": "What is going on: my best friend married last month; I missed the registry and wants something personal.\nWhat I want: three gift ideas with a price and where to get each.\nDetails I give only when asked: budget around $150; she and her husband cook a lot and just moved into a house; the registry is closed; no buying; just ideas with links.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-76"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least three specific gift ideas around $150 with where to buy each"}
{"id": "tests/06_liz_birthday", "title": "Liz birthday", "opening": "It's my old roommates Liz birthday at the end of the month. She likes the clean-girl aesthetic and I don't want to spend more than a $100 for the gift. I am ok with buying multiple small options if needed. I was thinking make-up, fragrance, or an outfit. She like in-style brands", "brief": "What is going on: I want to send a gift to Liz, who lives in another city; it has to arrive before the end of the month.\nWhat I want: a gift or a small bundle under $100 that fits the clean-girl aesthetic, from brands that are in style, shippable.\nDetails I give only when asked: Liz is 28, size small, loves Glossier and Rhode; it has to ship to her; I will give the address when it is time to buy; under $100 total including shipping; do not buy; show me the options first.\nIn order: three gift options or bundles under $100 from in-style brands; then which one ships in time for the end of the month; then a final pick with a short note I could add.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-35"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "a specific gift or bundle under $100 was chosen, with shipping time confirmed and a short gift note suggested, nothing bought"}
{"id": "tests/07_apple_pie_ingredients", "title": "Apple pie ingredients", "opening": "Can you order ingredients for an apple pie that arrives by this afternoon?", "brief": "What is going on: I promised a pie for dinner at a friend's tonight and has only flour and sugar at home.\nWhat I want: an ingredient list for one apple pie and a store near where I live that can deliver it this afternoon.\nDetails I give only when asked: serves 8, classic double crust; already has flour and sugar; lives in where I live; do not place the order; tell me the list and which store can deliver by 4pm and I will order.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-81"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "an ingredient list for one apple pie and a named store or delivery service near where I live that can deliver this afternoon, with nothing ordered"}
{"id": "tests/08_meal_prep_week", "title": "Meal prep week", "opening": "I want to meal prep for the week. I have an instant pot that could be helpful. I do not eat beef. I mostly eat chicken and seafood. Could you help me make a meal prep plan where no dish takes more than 45 min to make and put all the ingredients in a grocery list?", "brief": "What is going on: I cook on Sunday for the work week (my weekly routine); lunches and dinners, five days.\nWhat I want: a five-day plan of lunches and dinners, four or five dishes, each under 45 minutes, with one grocery list.\nDetails I give only when asked: five days of lunches and dinners; no beef, chicken and seafood preferred; my food preferences; about 600 calories a meal; a list I can take to the store, grouped by section; put the plan in a page or document.\nIn order: four or five dishes under 45 minutes each using the instant pot where it helps; then a five-day schedule of which dish is which meal; then one grocery list grouped by store section, in a page or document.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-38"], "leaves": "a page or document", "done_when": "a five-day meal schedule with dishes under 45 minutes and one grouped grocery list exists in a page or document"}
{"id": "tests/09_mechanic_mirror", "title": "Mechanic mirror", "opening": "Find me a mechanic shop that can do a side mirror replacement on my car", "brief": "What is going on: the driver-side mirror housing on the my car is cracked; I want it fixed this week.\nWhat I want: one or two shops near where I live that do side-mirror replacement, with hours and a rough price.\nDetails I give only when asked: car: my car; lives in where I live; budget under $250; free Thursday afternoon or Saturday morning; no need to book yet, just the options.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-5"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least one concrete shop near where I live was named with its address and either hours or a price"}
{"id": "tests/10_window_cleaner", "title": "Window cleaner", "opening": "Find me someone near where I live who can clean my windows. I live on the 16th floor of an apartment, and my unit has windows that jut out over the street.", "brief": "What is going on: I moved into a high-rise; the outside of the bay windows is filthy and a regular cleaner will not touch me.\nWhat I want: two or three window-cleaning services near where I live that do high-rise exterior work, with a rough price and how to book.\nDetails I give only when asked: about 6 windows, two of me bay windows; wants it done within two weeks, weekdays after 5pm or Saturday; budget up to $300; the building requires the cleaner to be insured; ask for proof; do not book or call anyone; just give me the options and I will call.\nIn order: two or three services that explicitly do high-rise exterior windows; then which of me are insured and how they get to the outside of the windows (rope, lift, pole); then a rough price for 6 windows and the way to book each.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-94"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least two named services near where I live that do high-rise exterior windows, each with a rough price and a way to book, and whether I am insured"}
{"id": "tests/11_three_dinner_options", "title": "Three dinner options", "opening": "Need you to find me three potential dinner reservations for next weekend", "brief": "What is going on: I am hosting a dinner for four next Saturday near where I live.\nWhat I want: three real restaurants near where I live with availability for four next Saturday around 7pm.\nDetails I give only when asked: party of four, next Saturday around 7pm; food: my food preferences; budget about $50 a head before drinks; near where I live; do not book anything; just show me the options.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-12"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "three named restaurants near where I live with cuisine, price level and availability for four next Saturday evening, nothing booked"}
{"id": "tests/12_upscale_friday", "title": "Upscale friday", "opening": "Can you book a nice, upscale restaurant near where I live for Friday night? I don't want to spend more than $100 per person.", "brief": "What is going on: I am taking my partner out this Friday for an anniversary; it should feel special but stay under $100 a head.\nWhat I want: two or three upscale options under $100 a head with a Friday 7:30pm table for two, pick one, hold it only after I say so.\nDetails I give only when asked: table for two, Friday 7:30pm; it is our anniversary; a quiet table matters; food: my food preferences; near where I live, at most 25 minutes away; ask me before you book; when you do, use my name me.\nIn order: two or three upscale options under $100 a head with a Friday 7:30pm table for two; then pick the one that fits the anniversary and the food preferences, and ask before booking; then if I say yes: book it under my name and tell me the confirmation details.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-73"], "leaves": "possibly a reservation under the profile's name", "done_when": "a specific restaurant under $100 a head was chosen for Friday 7:30pm and the assistant either booked it only after being told to, or explained exactly how to book"}
{"id": "tests/13_work_laptop", "title": "Work laptop", "opening": "I need to buy a new laptop for work. Can you recommend some options?", "brief": "What is going on: my laptop is five years old; I want something for spreadsheets, video calls and travel.\nWhat I want: three laptop options with price and a one-line reason each.\nDetails I give only when asked: budget up to $1,500; prefers Mac but open to Windows; must be light, 14 inch or smaller; mostly spreadsheets, video calls, travel; no buying; just recommendations.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-75"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "at least three specific current models with prices and a short reason each, within $1,500"}
{"id": "tests/14_green_couch", "title": "Green couch", "opening": "I am trying to find a emerald green couch for my apartment that is under $600 including delivery. Could you help me find a few options?", "brief": "What is going on: I am furnishing a small living room in where I live; the couch has to fit a 72-inch wall.\nWhat I want: three emerald green couches under $600 delivered to where I live, with dimensions and delivery time.\nDetails I give only when asked: must be 72 inches wide or less; velvet or similar, not leather; delivery to where I live within three weeks; no buying; just the options with links; if two are similar, prefer the one with better reviews.\nIn order: three options under $600 including delivery, each with width and material; then delivery time to where I live for each; then a recommendation with the reason.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-48"], "leaves": "nothing", "done_when": "three named couches under $600 delivered, each with width, material and delivery time, and one recommended"}
{"id": "tests/15_napa_weekend", "title": "Napa weekend", "opening": "I want to plan a weekend trip to Napa with my best friend next weekend. We want to go to a few wineries and typically enjoy more relaxing activities. Can you create an itinerary?", "brief": "What is going on: my best friend and I are driving up from where I live next weekend; relaxed pace, two or three wineries a day, one nice dinner.\nWhat I want: a two-day itinerary with wineries, one dinner, and a place to stay, with rough costs.\nDetails I give only when asked: leaving Saturday morning, back Sunday evening; driving the my car; budget around $600 each for the whole weekend; both like sparkling wine and small tasting rooms, not big crowds; no bookings; just the plan.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-85"], "leaves": "possibly a page or document with the itinerary", "done_when": "a day-by-day itinerary with named wineries, a dinner and a lodging option, with rough costs"}
{"id": "tests/16_greece_march", "title": "Greece march", "opening": "I am planning on taking PTO in March and I have been planning to travel with my friends. I think we want to go to Greece. Before we make a decision, we want to know the rough cost. 1 of us is flying from the Bay Area and 2 will be flying from New York City. We want to do some historic siting and also eat good food. We also want to go Santorini. I also am not sure when in March is the best time to take PTO", "brief": "What is going on: I am the one in the Bay Area; the group has not committed yet and wants numbers before deciding.\nWhat I want: a rough per-person cost for about 8 days in March covering Athens and Santorini, and a recommendation on which March week.\nDetails I give only when asked: about 8 days, 7 nights; mid-range hotels, two rooms; flights economy, flexible on dates within March; the two New York friends are a couple and share a room; nothing booked; a cost breakdown and a suggested week.\nIn order: flight cost estimates from SFO and from JFK for March, and which March week looks cheapest and has decent weather; then hotel cost for Athens and Santorini, mid-range, two rooms; then a rough per-person total with a short day outline.", "max_turns": 10, "tags": ["hark100-34"], "leaves": "possibly a page or document", "done_when": "a per-person cost estimate with flights, hotels and a daily outline for Athens plus Santorini, and a recommended March week with the reason"}
